{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And Elohim saw the light, that it was good.</b> And so it was: Elohim saw and chose its existence for the sake of the end — the good — for whose sake He had brought it into being by His active knowing." "<b>And Elohim separated between the light and between the darkness.</b> Those days in which the first light served were times of light and times of darkness — not by the rotation of a sphere, but by divine will that separated the time of light from the time of darkness."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:11:13.358754138Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}